 "funeral": {
  "scriptedBurial": {
   "found": true,
   "respectsOk": true,
   "buryOk": true,
   "buried": true
  },
  "deathBeat": [
   "d10: 📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Caleb Bauer is dead. You didn't ask. It knew.",
   "d10: 🕯️ Caleb Bauer is dead — the arena. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging."
  ],
  "recoverHome": [
   "d11: That night, they bring Caleb home. Nobody asks you to help carry; nobody has to. By morning the grave is dug by the fire, and the body is laid out beside it. The filling of it is yours."
  ],
  "vouch": [],
  "systemVoice": [
   "d10: SYSTEM: \"Perimeter violated! This is unprecedented! ...Is this unprecedented? Checking. Yes. Unprecedented.\"",
   "d10: SYSTEM: \"INTRUDER REPELLED. The pantry’s aroma is now classified as a defensive liability. The audience is chanting the defenders’ names. Fan clubs are forming. This is how it starts.\"",
   "d10: ◈ SYSTEM: \"Ooh. NEIGHBORS. You know what neighbors are for? STORYLINES. Go knock — worst case, it's CONTENT. Best case? The show gets BIGGER.\"",
   "d10: ◈ AUDIENCE TRIAL — SYSTEM: \"The audience wants an encore. A trial, then — smaller this time, but televised.\" Haul 1,000 kcal to the pantry within 3 days. Reward: integration, and a lesson.",
   "d10: ◈ ARC III — ENGINES. SYSTEM: \"VIEWERSHIP MILESTONE. Organic unit demonstrates compounding capability. Resonance protocols unlocked.\" — Your gifts deepen. Used in sequence, they resonate. The village is no longer just surviving. It is becoming something."
  ],
  "burialWindowSay": [
   "d10: ◈ The System files the name away with visible satisfaction. It has so few words for things that bleed. (+5 integration)",
   "d11: That night, they bring Caleb home. Nobody asks you to help carry; nobody has to. By morning the grave is dug by the fire, and the body is laid out beside it. The filling of it is yours.",
   "d12: ◈ The System files the name away with visible satisfaction. It has so few words for things that bleed. (+4 integration)",
   "d13: You say a few words for Caleb. Not a ceremony — just: you were here, and someone noticed you leaving. (-3 trauma)",
   "d13: You bury Caleb. A marker, of sorts. The village will know where. (+4 trauma)",
   "d13: ◈ CRISIS — THE FIRST GRAVE. Nolan is dead. The village digs its first grave, and everyone understands at once: this place can kill you. It just did."
  ],
  "pendingBurialsLeft": 0,
